1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:04,750
Bookmakers gave Leicester City a 5000–1 chance… of winning the Premier League.

2
00:00:04,850 --> 00:00:09,950
A year earlier, they’d spent Christmas bottom of the table… and only just escaped relegation.

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:14,200
Then they hired Claudio Ranieri. Most predictions still had them going down.

4
00:00:14,250 --> 00:00:18,700
But Jamie Vardy scored in 11 Premier League games in a row… a new record.

5
00:00:18,750 --> 00:00:23,450
Riyad Mahrez danced past defenders. N’Golo Kanté won the ball back everywhere.

6
00:00:23,550 --> 00:00:26,050
By Christmas… Leicester were top.

7
00:00:26,100 --> 00:00:28,150
May 2, 2016.

8
00:00:28,200 --> 00:00:32,950
The players gathered at Vardy’s house to watch Chelsea v Tottenham. Spurs had to win.

9
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:36,400
2–0 Tottenham at half-time… then Chelsea fought back.

10
00:00:36,450 --> 00:00:38,550
Eden Hazard… 2–2.

11
00:00:38,600 --> 00:00:42,300
Leicester were champions, for the first time in their 132-year history.

12
00:00:42,350 --> 00:00:48,500
Biggest shock in sport… or can you name a bigger one?
